  "notes": "First-cut local removable-media fallback: host-controlled read-only mount feeds a disposable no-network ingest jail through a read-only mount.view after fstyp admits exfat under a finite allowlist; the ingest walk stays physical and root-pinned beneath /ingest, admits only regular files plus explicit directories, fails closed on symlink/device/FIFO/socket semantics, does not preserve hardlink topology in the first cut, member paths normalize to relative-clean Unicode NFC text, normalization collisions fail closed, there is no silent auto-rename or source-prefix repair, the ingest jail receives no raw block device nodes, /ingest stays inert input only, and there is no direct host-open or execution from the mounted tree, keeps path/kind/payload-first reviewed/import identity, keeps owner/mode/mtime/xattr fidelity out of scope in the first cut, and treats any receiver-local metadata outcomes as receiver-local realization detail rather than portable reviewed state. This first lane stays single-selected-subject only, the selected subject stays regular-file-only in the first cut, directories are not selectable import subjects in this lane, direct multi-member review/import is out of scope in the first cut, and multiple outputs only arise as a deterministic consequence of processing that one selected subject; in this first cut that subject is the selected regular file. Approval for this flow stays present-device-instance-only in the first cut; physical detach or lease end revokes it, and reattaching the same nominal medium requires a fresh grant even when serial or disk-ident hints look the same. The canonical attach receipt for this lane keeps a finite current-presence hint bundle (`ugen`/provider plus disk-ident or physical-path hints when available), explicitly marks those hints evidence-only, and keeps same-hints-on-reattach non-authoritative. Once one selected regular file is chosen, the first non-browsing step is capture-first into disposable /work staging, later operations do not consume the live mounted /ingest path, and capture failure or digest mismatch fails closed. Once capture verifies, the preserved capture must commit into authoritative quarantine store before detach, later operations restart in a fresh post-detach worker with /ingest absent and with no inherited file-descriptor/current-working-directory/root references to the old mount, and those later operations read a read-only projection of the stored preserved capture rather than the old scratch path. After verified capture and detach, the preserved capture remains exact evidence in authoritative quarantine store, later classify/scan/sanitize steps must not rewrite that capture in place, and any sanitized output is a separate derivative from the preserved capture. After detach, later operations receive the stored preserved capture only through a single-object synthetic projection path, not through a browseable authoritative-store namespace. That worker-visible projection path is only plumbing: before later operations begin it must bind to the preserved selected subject digest, the launcher/broker must prepare it as one launcher-preopened read-only object (or equivalent), later operations must not reacquire the subject through broader path or store lookup, and the canonical receipt must record that digest-bound delivery explicitly. Later-worker derivative bytes must leave through launcher-precreated disposable outbox sink objects, `/work/output/...` stays execution plumbing rather than authoritative derivative identity, the first lane admits only one declared writable derivative slot, extra worker result surface stays out, and the launcher/broker must collect + remeasure the bytes from that declared slot before the canonical receipt names the derivative authoritatively. The launcher/broker must still collect + remeasure those bytes before the canonical receipt names the derivative authoritatively. The one declared writable derivative slot starts as a launcher-precreated empty regular file, the launcher hands it to the later worker already opened O_APPEND, keeps it append-only-protected while the worker runs, omits CAP_READ/CAP_FTRUNCATE/CAP_FCNTL from worker authority, and treats any CAP_SEEK on that seekable file as implementation ballast rather than rewrite authority, so derivative egress stays append-open with no worker readback or truncate. The launcher or its approved shim must enter capability mode before handing control to later classify/scan/sanitize tool code, descendants inherit that mode and may not clear it, no ambient absolute-path opens remain after cap_enter, and any tool that cannot run on the preopened capability set stays out of this first lane unless a later explicit wrapper/broker contract earns it. After capability mode entry, later tool code inherits only the reviewed descriptor set; the launcher closes or spawn-closefroms every non-reviewed descriptor before handoff, stdin stays inert null/empty input only, stdout/stderr stay launcher-owned observation channels or reviewed append-only log sinks, and no parent TTY/session socket is inherited into this first lane. The post-detach executable identity is launcher-resolved and digest-pinned (launcher-resolved-executable-digest-no-path-search); no PATH/cwd/media-derived executable lookup is admitted, the wrapper contract digest is receipt-visible, and implicit helper/plugin discovery stays out (no-implicit-helper-or-plugin-discovery). Post-detach worker credentials are launcher-fixed and unprivileged: launcher-fixed-unprivileged-credential-envelope-no-supplementary-groups; worker user/group are derive-rm-worker:derive-rm-worker, supplementary groups stay absent, and no-setuid-setgid-saved-id-or-ambient-privilege-regain. Post-detach later work also runs under a launcher-enforced resource envelope: CPU time, wall clock, memory, open-file count, process count, scratch bytes, and declared derivative-output bytes are bounded before execution; resource-limit hits fail closed and do not yield derivative receipt authority. Post-detach peer interaction stays launcher-isolated: launcher-isolated-peer-envelope-no-ambient-ptrace-signal-or-ipc; signal control is launcher-only-signal-control-no-peer-or-session-control; IPC/procfs exposure is no-unreviewed-ipc-sockets-shm-pipes-or-procfs and procfs-ptrace-and-ktrace-unavailable-to-worker-and-peers, so same-UID peers, parent sessions, procfs/ptrace/ktrace, sockets, shared memory, and unreviewed pipes cannot become hidden control or observation authority. Post-detach network egress stays absent: network-egress-absent-no-socket-dns-or-remote-callbacks, receipt-records-network-absent-envelope, no-dns-mdns-nss-or-resolver-host-input, no-proxy-or-remote-service-configuration, and no-remote-fetch-or-callback-derivative-authority keep DNS/NSS, proxy configuration, remote fetches, and callbacks out of ordinary derivative authority. Post-detach persistent state stays absent: persistent-state-absent-no-home-cache-or-host-state-writes; the launcher records receipt-records-persistent-state-absence-and-scratch-cleanup, any scratch is launcher-created-empty-scratch-nonauthoritative, cleanup is scratch-destroyed-before-derivative-receipt, and no-user-home-cache-config-or-history-state keeps user-home/cache/config/history writes out of ordinary derivative authority. After r507, derivative receipt queryability is a redacted lease-gated projection: typed-post-detach-query-projection-positive-and-negative-fixture-guarded keeps raw media paths, observed hints, host identity, filenames, and body text out of ambient indexes."
